  "tagline": "Pioneering embeddable object database for Java and .NET, discontinued by Actian in 2014.",
  "description": "db4o was an open-source embedded object database for Java and .NET that stored plain objects directly, with no mapping layer, and offered native queries, query-by-example, SODA and LINQ. In the late 2000s it was a common choice for embedded devices and early Android apps. Versant acquired db4objects in 2008, Actian acquired Versant in 2012, and Actian ended development and support in 2014. Only community mirrors of the old code remain. It belongs in the catalogue for history and migrations. Today's closest equivalents are ObjectBox, Realm or plain SQLite.",
